    "Phase 3 held-out set. Selected and sealed on 2026-11-26 BEFORE any phase 3 engine change, at RedWall",
    "commit 8b17a8c (main after phase 2). The selection protocol is in README.md next to this file.",
    "`ref` is the parent of the fix commit (the vulnerable tree), `fixed_ref` the fix commit itself. Line numbers",
    "are at `ref` and relative to the repository root. `sources` is where attacker data enters Python code;",
    "`sinks` is where the vulnerable operation happens; `via` lists intermediate files the flow passes through",
    "(informational). `shared: true` marks a generic helper sink every caller reaches.",
    "Rules for this file: run it only to measure a finished change (before/after), report aggregate numbers,",
    "never look at per-case misses to design or tune a rule. The sha256 in SEAL must match; run.py refuses",
    "to score a modified manifest unless --allow-unsealed is passed (and then marks the run as unsealed)."
